[[6,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Place the car on a ramp.</p>"],[2,127,0,"<p>1. Disconnect the electrical connection for the rpm and timing sensor.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Rpm sensor</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3236554\">K46</a></p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018648.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2,127,0,"<p>Disconnect the electrical connection for\nthe rpm and timing sensor on the side part of the air intake casing (VIS\ndevice), timing side.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Rpm sensor</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3236554\">K46</a></p></td></tr></table></div>"],[6,127,0,"<p>Raise the car.</p><p><a href=\"#/3238966\">7055B54</a></p><p>1. Undo the bolts and remove the rpm and timing sensor together\nwith its wiring.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018649.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[6,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Fit the rpm and timing sensor together\nwith its wiring to the crankcase and tighten the retaining bolt.</p><p><a href=\"#/3238966\">7055B54</a></p><p>Lower the vehicle.</p>"],[2,127,0,"<p>Connect the electrical connection for the\nrpm and timing sensor to the connector located on the side of the\nair intake casing (VIS device), timing side.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Rpm sensor</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3236554\">K46</a></p></td></tr></table></div>"],[2,127,0,"<p>Connect the electrical connection for the\nrpm and timing sensor to the connector fastened to the air intake\ncasing from the  timing side.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Rpm sensor</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3236554\">K46</a></p></td></tr></table></div>"],[16,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/3238429\">5530B10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3237573\">1076B52</a></p><p>1. Remove flywheel protection ( 1a) and rpm sensor by unscrewing\nthe three bolts (1b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018650.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[16,127,0,"<p>1. Unscrew retaining bolts (1a) and remove rpm sensor (1b) from\nits seat.  Then release lead (1c) from the core hitches fastened\nto the body.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018651.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[16,127,0,"<p>1. Working from inside the engine bay, disconnect the electrical\nconnection and withdraw the rpm sensor.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Rpm sensor</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3236554\">K46</a></p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018652.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[16,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>1. Fit the engine rpm sensor and secure to the crankcase. Use a\nfeeler gauge to check that the gap between sensor and engine flywheel\nis 0.8 - 1.5mm.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Feeler gauge</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.895.113.000</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018653.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[16,127,0,"<p>Connect the electrical connection and secure\nthe electrical lead to the core hitches on the engine.</p><p>Fit the engine flywheel protection and\nsecuring using bolts.</p><p><a href=\"#/3237573\">1076B52</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238429\">5530B10</a></p>"],[264,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Ensure that the ignition key is in the\nOFF position, then disconnect the negative battery terminal (-).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Battery</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3235044\">A1B</a></p></td></tr></table></div><p>Proceed with removal \n                                          <a href=\"#/3238966\">7055B54</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Proceed with removal \n                                          <a href=\"#/3237704\">1076B18</a>\n                                           .</p><p>1. Disconnect the electrical connection for the rpm sensor.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Rpm sensor</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3236554\">K46</a></p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Undo the bolt (2a) and remove the rpm sensor (2b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018654.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[264,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>1. Place the rpm sensor (1a) in its seating and secure it tightening\nthe bolt (1b) to the specified torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>RPM SENSOR</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Engine crankcase side) 0.8 ÷ 1.0</p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Connect the electrical connection for the rpm sensor.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018655.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[264,127,0,"<p>Proceed with refitting \n                                          <a href=\"#/3237704\">1076B18</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Proceed with refitting \n                                          <a href=\"#/3238966\">7055B54</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Connect the negative (-) battery terminal.</p><p>Remove the car from the ramps.</p>"]]